  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Friday)\nIssued at 1038 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nHigh pressure remains in place Saturday night and Sunday morning. \nThis will provide another chilly night, with additional frost and/or \nfog potential expected for NE OK and NW AR. In fact, a brief freeze \nwill be possible for the typical colder spots along the OK-KS border \nand in far NW AR as winds go calm. This potential will need to be \nmonitored, and a Freeze Warning may be needed. Given these \nconditions, at least a brief period of patchy freezing fog cannot be \nruled out Sunday morning.\n\nDry conditions are favored early next week as high pressure remains \nin the area before drifting southeast. This will permit a return of \nsoutherly winds on Monday with warming temperatures. A few isolated \nshowers are possible across SE OK on Tuesday as an upper low moves \nalong the Red River, but any rainfall will remain light. By midweek, \na cold front will push through the region, bringing temperatures \nback down to average and perhaps sparking some precipitation over \neastern portions of the FA. From here, deep troughing develops over \nthe E CONUS through the end of the week w/ sfc high pressure over\nthe CWA. This is likely to keep the area dry and cool through \nnext weekend.",
